From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: honour msm.enable_preemption=0

A5xx GPUs other than A510 always get four rings and preemption, and the
enable_preemption module parameter only applies to A7xx. Let
enable_preemption=0 give A5xx a single ring, i.e. no preemption, so it
can be ruled in or out when chasing faults.

On the Mi MIX (Adreno 530) GPU translation faults show up only while two
GPU clients run at once (KWin at high priority with a browser, or during
a rotation), the faulting addresses being buffers freed shortly before.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
 #include "msm_mmu.h"
 #include "a5xx_gpu.h"
 
+extern int enable_preemption;
+
 extern bool hang_debug;
 static void a5xx_dump(struct msm_gpu *gpu);
 
@@ -1750,7 +1752,11 @@
 
 	nr_rings = 4;
 
-	if (config->info->revn == 510)
+	/*
+	 * One ring means no preemption: A510 cannot do it, and
+	 * msm.enable_preemption=0 turns it off on the others.
+	 */
+	if (config->info->revn == 510 || enable_preemption == 0)
 		nr_rings = 1;
 
 	ret = adreno_gpu_init(dev, pdev, adreno_gpu, config->info->funcs, nr_rings);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 module_param_named(snapshot_debugbus, snapshot_debugbus, bool, 0600);
 
 int enable_preemption = -1;
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_preemption, "Enable preemption (A7xx only) (1=on , 0=disable, -1=auto (default))");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_preemption, "Enable preemption (A7xx; 0 also disables it on A5xx) (1=on , 0=disable, -1=auto (default))");
 module_param(enable_preemption, int, 0600);
 
 bool disable_acd;
